## RESULT: PASS
App negotiates the exchange layout from the app device's TRUE caps (LINEAR fallback,
accepted by the game device), imports 2 staging images, creates 2 self-exporting dest
images, opens a backend cross-device context, verifies isCrossDevice()==true, and logs
"context created ... cross-device=1" on all 20 streams. Full handshake completes across
10 rapid churns with a single listener, fd stable (9->9), and ZERO VUID.

## Fix log (deviation from the mechanical spec)
1. negotiateExchangeLayout app-vs-app (RADV vs RADV) returned a RADV-only proper DRM
   modifier (0x144115188076389125) that the ANV game device rejected ("negotiated
   modifier ... not advertised by game device"), breaking the stream before READY.
   Fixed: negotiate against a LINEAR-only caps proxy (mirror layer swapchain.cpp),
   forcing modifier == EXCHANGE_MODIFIER_LINEAR so the game device accepts it.
2. The original (pre-fix) path only closed the exportDmaBuf handle on the dup-failure
   branch; the success path leaked one unowned fd per dest image (2/stream). Confirmed
   leak 9->49 over 20 streams. Fixed: close exp.fd after the dup is handed to the
   backend (backend only consumes the dup), restoring fd stability 9->9.
